{"url":"https://aphrody.app/","title":"Aphrody Bun","body":"Aphrody\nBun\n\n\nRuntime\nDocs\nDownloads\nRelease notes\nBenchmarks\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAphrody Labs\n\n\n\nBun OS\n\n\n\nThe Bun runtime of Aphrody. JavaScript and TypeScript runtime, package manager, test runner and bundler in one executable, with Aphrody's native system integrations.\n\n\n\n\naphrody-labs/bun builds on oven-sh/bun 1.4.4. Source version and published executables are tracked separately; published release: aphrody-v1.4.3-aphrody.4.\n\n\n\n\nInstall a published runtime:\n\n\n\nLinux and macOS (bash)\ncurl -fsSL https://aphrody.app/install | bash\nWindows (PowerShell)\npowershell -c \"irm aphrody.app/install.ps1|iex\"\nnpm\nnpm install -g @aphrody/bun-runtime\n\n\nDocumentation\nDownloads\nGitHub\n\n\n\n\nOne executable for your workflow\n\n\n\nUse the tools individually in an existing project, or build your application around Bun.\n\n\n\n\n\nRuntime\n\nRun JavaScript, TypeScript and JSX on JavaScriptCore. Explore the documented Node.js and Web APIs.\n\nbun run index.tsx\nCopy\nRuntime docs\n\n\nPackage manager\n\nInstall npm packages, manage workspaces and keep dependencies in a Bun lockfile.\n\nbun install\nCopy\nPackage manager docs\n\n\nTest runner\n\nWrite tests with assertions, mocks and snapshots from bun:test.\n\nbun test\nCopy\nTest runner docs\n\n\nBundler\n\nBundle JavaScript, TypeScript, JSX and CSS for browser or runtime targets.\n\nbun build ./app.tsx --outdir dist\nCopy\nBundler docs\n\n\n\n\nNative integrations from Aphrody Labs\n\n\n\nSystem modules, Python and .NET hosting, graph APIs and desktop integration live alongside the Bun toolkit. Platform requirements and source inventory are documented in the runtime reference.\n\n\n\n\nPackages use the @aphrody npm scope. Built-in imports keep their identities: bun, bun:sqlite, bun:test and platform modules. Rust crates retain their manifest and ABI names.\n\n\n\n\nThe Bun OS stable release is pending native factory build and test qualification. See published releases and checksums for the executables currently available.\n\n\n\n\n\nCurrent versions\n\n\n\n\n\n\nItem\nVersion\nSource\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPublished runtime\n1.4.3-aphrody.4\naphrody-v1.4.3-aphrody.4\n\n\nSource\n1.4.4 · d9cbd5c9e2c9 (2026-10-12)\naphrody-labs/bun\n\n\nUpstream\nlast merge c1de6f2335 (2026-10-09)\noven-sh/bun\n\n\nFork commits\n773 since 2026-10-02 (merge commits excluded)\nRuntime\n\n\nnpm\n@aphrody/bun-runtime 1.4.3-aphrody.2\nnpmjs.com\n\n\n\n\n\n\nRole in Aphrody\n\n\n\naphrody-labs/bun is the runtime component of Aphrody. Every runtime change Aphrody needs is made in this repository, as a commit on main. The Aphrody product repository (aphrody-labs/aphrody) has no Bun patch queue, no vendored copy of Bun and no Rust copy of Bun code. It uses the artifacts below.\n\n\n\n\nThe runtime also owns the system layer. That covers Windows and Linux APIs, FFI, native libraries, the system Rust crates, and .NET, C and C++ interop. The product consumes this layer; it does not keep its own copy (docs/aphrody/LAYERS.md).\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nArtifact\nSource in this repository\nConsumer in Aphrody\n\n\n\n\n\n\nRuntime binary\naphrody-v* GitHub releases; npm @aphrody/bun-runtime (scripts/aphrody/publi","links":[{"text":"AphrodyBun","href":"https://aphrody.app/"},{"text":"Runtime","href":"https://aphrody.app/runtime"},{"text":"Docs","href":"https://aphrody.app/docs"},{"text":"Downloads","href":"https://aphrody.app/downloads"},{"text":"Release notes","href":"https://aphrody.app/release-notes"},{"text":"Benchmarks","href":"https://aphrody.app/benchmarks"},{"text":"GitHub","href":"https://github.com/aphrody-labs/bun"},{"text":"aphrody-labs/bun","href":"https://github.com/aphrody-labs/bun"},{"text":"oven-sh/bun","href":"https://github.com/oven-sh/bun"},{"text":"aphrody-v1.4.3-aphrody.4","href":"https://github.com/aphrody-labs/bun/releases/tag/aphrody-v1.4.3-aphrody.4"},{"text":"Documentation","href":"https://aphrody.app/docs"},{"te